---

<AnswerPage title="Downright vs Marked" trail="Downright vs Marked" updated={reviewedLabel} description={pageMeta.marked.description} markdownPath={pageMeta.marked.markdownPath ?? "/compare/marked.md"}>
  <p>Marked is a dedicated Markdown preview application for Mac workflows that already have an editor. Downright combines preview, editing, source inspection, and external-change review in one native app.</p>

  <h2>Choose Downright if…</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need to edit the Markdown as well as read its rendered form.</li>
    <li>You want a native file watcher and word-level review for agent rewrites.</li>
    <li>You want Quick Look, Finder, Spotlight, and the <code>down</code> CLI in the same product.</li>
    <li>You prefer a free MIT-licensed application with no account requirement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Choose Marked if…</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You already have a writing editor and want a dedicated preview companion.</li>
    <li>You value Marked's existing export, style, and editor integration workflow.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The practical difference</h2>
  <p>Marked is a preview specialist. Downright is a file-aware Markdown workspace for reading, editing, rendering, and reviewing files that other processes may change.</p>

  <p class="answer-sources">Reviewed/tested {reviewedLabel}. Primary references: <a href="https://marked2app.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Marked’s official site</a> and the <a href="/markdown-editor-mac-free/">full editor comparison</a>. Features and pricing can change; use the official site as the current source.</p>
</AnswerPage>
